1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,360
Read a simple A1 article about bakeries.

2
00:00:03,620 --> 00:00:10,640
Learn what bakeries sell, how people choose food, and how bakeries can feel different in Japan and other countries.

3
00:00:11,440 --> 00:00:13,780
Then practice ordering in a role play.

4
00:00:14,300 --> 00:00:16,420
Do you buy bread or snacks at a bakery?

5
00:00:17,380 --> 00:00:18,960
What bakery food do you know?

6
00:00:19,600 --> 00:00:21,960
Do bakeries look different in different countries?

7
00:00:23,060 --> 00:00:25,340
A bakery makes or sells baked food.

8
00:00:25,340 --> 00:00:31,200
Many bakeries sell bread, rolls, cakes, sandwiches, and pastries.

9
00:00:31,740 --> 00:00:36,880
Some bakeries bake early in the morning, so people can buy fresh food before work or school.

10
00:00:37,740 --> 00:00:42,960
A bakery can be a quick stop, but it can also be a quiet place to choose something special.

11
00:00:44,540 --> 00:00:48,520
In many bakeries, food is behind glass or on open shelves.

12
00:00:49,280 --> 00:00:54,060
People look at the display case, compare prices, and choose one or two things.

13
00:00:54,060 --> 00:00:57,380
If they do not know the food name, they can point.

14
00:00:57,940 --> 00:01:00,820
The important thing is to be clear and polite.

15
00:01:01,220 --> 00:01:04,060
In Japan, many bakeries have trays and tongs.

16
00:01:04,780 --> 00:01:09,120
Customers often pick up a tray, choose bread or pastries, and take the tray to the counter.

17
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:14,640
Some bakeries sell soft breads, curry bread, melon bread, and small sandwiches.

18
00:01:15,440 --> 00:01:19,560
Many people choose takeaway, but some bakeries also have a small seating area.

19
00:01:20,440 --> 00:01:22,540
Bakeries can feel different in other countries.

20
00:01:22,540 --> 00:01:26,220
In France, people may buy baguettes and croissants.

21
00:01:26,940 --> 00:01:29,740
In Germany, people may choose dark bread or pretzels.

22
00:01:30,280 --> 00:01:34,320
In the United States, some bakeries sell bagels, muffins, and cookies.

23
00:01:34,960 --> 00:01:41,340
The food changes, but the basic action is similar: choose, order, pay, and take the food.

24
00:01:42,600 --> 00:01:45,060
A customer talks to a bakery worker in the morning.

25
00:01:45,680 --> 00:01:49,440
Useful role-play phrases: This one, please.

26
00:01:49,460 --> 00:01:50,740
How much is this?

27
00:01:51,040 --> 00:01:51,820
For here or takeaway?

28
00:01:53,160 --> 00:01:53,860
Takeaway, please.

29
00:01:54,380 --> 00:01:55,440
I will pay by card.

30
00:01:56,120 --> 00:01:57,100
Can I have a receipt?

31
00:01:58,360 --> 00:01:59,060
At the bakery:

32
00:01:59,860 --> 00:02:00,560
Good morning.

33
00:02:00,860 --> 00:02:01,660
Do you have sandwiches?

34
00:02:02,460 --> 00:02:03,160
Yes.

35
00:02:03,180 --> 00:02:05,280
We have egg sandwiches and chicken sandwiches.

36
00:02:05,940 --> 00:02:07,270
One egg sandwich, please.

37
00:02:07,480 --> 00:02:08,180
Sure.

38
00:02:08,440 --> 00:02:09,160
Anything else?

39
00:02:09,400 --> 00:02:10,420
This roll looks nice.

40
00:02:10,620 --> 00:02:11,840
How much is it?

41
00:02:11,980 --> 00:02:13,440
It is two dollars.

42
00:02:13,460 --> 00:02:14,720
I will take one roll too.

43
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:15,840
For here or takeaway?

44
00:02:17,120 --> 00:02:17,890
Takeaway, please.

45
00:02:18,120 --> 00:02:19,660
That is seven dollars.

46
00:02:19,680 --> 00:02:20,860
I will pay by card.

47
00:02:22,360 --> 00:02:23,060
Thank you.

48
00:02:23,440 --> 00:02:25,630
Here is your receipt.

49
00:02:26,080 --> 00:02:27,940
What does a bakery make or sell?

50
00:02:28,760 --> 00:02:34,940
A bakery makes or sells baked food, such as bread, rolls, cakes, sandwiches, and pastries.

51
00:02:36,020 --> 00:02:37,700
What bakery food do you like?

52
00:02:38,560 --> 00:02:41,200
What can people do if they do not know the food name?

53
00:02:41,360 --> 00:02:42,680
They can point to the food.

54
00:02:43,120 --> 00:02:45,080
What food would you point to in a bakery?

55
00:02:45,080 --> 00:02:48,800
What do many customers use in Japanese bakeries?

56
00:02:49,140 --> 00:02:51,720
They use trays and tongs.

57
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:54,620
What Japanese bakery food would you like to try?

58
00:02:55,400 --> 00:02:57,720
What action is similar in many bakeries?

59
00:02:57,980 --> 00:03:00,700
People choose, order, pay, and take the food.

60
00:03:01,020 --> 00:03:04,040
Which country's bakery food sounds interesting to you?

61
00:03:04,900 --> 00:03:06,380
What does the customer buy?

62
00:03:06,940 --> 00:03:10,100
The customer buys an egg sandwich and one roll.

63
00:03:10,940 --> 00:03:11,860
Practice the role play.

64
00:03:11,860 --> 00:03:15,160
Then change the food or payment method.

65
00:03:34,320 --> 00:03:37,040
Bakeries are common, but they are not the same everywhere.

66
00:03:37,640 --> 00:03:44,020
Japan, France, Germany, the United States, and many other places have different bakery foods and customs.

67
00:03:44,860 --> 00:03:54,600
Still, the simple English path is useful everywhere: choose the food, ask a clear question, say for here or takeaway, and pay.
